WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.541
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:05.221
Dad?

00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:07.316
Sam. This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:07.351 --> 00:00:09.404
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:09.439 --> 00:00:11.668
Saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:11.703 --> 00:00:13.175
The family business.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.648
I got to find dad.

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:17.578
I dreamt about Jessica's
death before it happened.

00:00:17.613 --> 00:00:18.543
You got to be careful, all right?

00:00:18.578 --> 00:00:21.164
Ghosts are attracted to that
whole ESP thing you got going.

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:23.580
I told you I don't have ESP.
I just have strange vibes.

00:00:23.615 --> 00:00:26.801
Weird dreams. Dead people
have weird dreams, man.

00:00:26.836 --> 00:00:29.987
I have these nightmares.
Sometimes they come true.

00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:31.587
Come again?

00:02:00.346 --> 00:02:02.736
Somebody help me! Somebody...!

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.177
Somebody help...!

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:36.683
Dean.

00:02:37.942 --> 00:02:39.211
Dean.

00:02:41.877 --> 00:02:44.438
What are you doing, man? It's
in the middle of the night.

00:02:44.656 --> 00:02:46.428
We have to go.

00:02:46.603 --> 00:02:48.685
What's happening? We have to go.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.218
Right now.

00:02:54.913 --> 00:02:55.795
Mcreedy.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.205
Detective Mcreedy. Badge number 158.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.621
I've got a signal four
eighty on progress.

00:03:00.656 --> 00:03:04.124
I need a registered
owner of a Two door Sedan.

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:07.592
Michigan license plate
Mary, Frank, 6-0-3-7.

00:03:07.627 --> 00:03:09.069
Yeah, okay. Just hurry.

00:03:09.104 --> 00:03:10.473
Sammy, relax.

00:03:10.508 --> 00:03:13.758
I'm sure, its just a nightmare.
Yeah. Tell me about it.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:17.008
I mean it. You know, a normal
everyday naked class nightmare.

00:03:17.043 --> 00:03:19.359
This license plate, it
won't check out. You'll see.

00:03:19.394 --> 00:03:21.270
It felt different Dean. Real.

00:03:21.305 --> 00:03:23.726
Like we dreamt about our
old house and Jessica.

00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:26.612
Oh, yeah. That makes sense. Dreaming
about our house, your girlfriend.

00:03:26.647 --> 00:03:28.471
This guy in your dream,
you ever seen him before?

00:03:28.506 --> 00:03:30.003
No... No, exactly.

00:03:30.038 --> 00:03:32.687
Why would you have premonitions
about some random dude in Michigan?

00:03:32.722 --> 00:03:34.044
I don't know. Yeah, me neither.

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:35.475
Yes, I'm here.

00:03:39.143 --> 00:03:41.718
Jim Miller, Saginaw Michigan.

00:03:41.753 --> 00:03:44.294
You have the street address?

00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:47.450
Got it. Thanks.

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.139
It checks out.

00:03:51.174 --> 00:03:52.768
How far are we?

00:03:53.759 --> 00:03:55.086
From Saginaw? Yeah.

00:03:55.121 --> 00:03:56.799
A couple of hours.

00:03:58.507 --> 00:04:00.403
Drive faster.

00:04:51.171 --> 00:04:52.659
What happened?

00:04:52.694 --> 00:04:54.645
Suicide.

00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:58.022
I can't believe it.

00:04:59.977 --> 00:05:01.591
Did you know him?

00:05:01.626 --> 00:05:05.390
Saw him everyday at Saint Augustine.

00:05:05.425 --> 00:05:09.155
Always seems... seemed so normal.

00:05:09.331 --> 00:05:12.413
I guess you never know what's
going behind closed doors.

00:05:12.448 --> 00:05:15.107
I guess not. How did uh...

00:05:15.142 --> 00:05:17.732
What are they saying happened?

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.812
I heard they found him in the garage

00:05:19.847 --> 00:05:23.463
Locked inside his car
with the engine running.

00:05:24.327 --> 00:05:26.444
Do you know about what
time they found him?

00:05:26.479 --> 00:05:29.158
It just happened an hour or two ago.

00:05:29.193 --> 00:05:31.141
His poor family.

00:05:31.176 --> 00:05:34.950
I can't even imagine what
they're going through.

00:05:53.221 --> 00:05:54.829
Sam, we got here as fast as we could.

00:05:54.864 --> 00:05:56.955
Not fast enough.

00:05:57.585 --> 00:06:00.106
Which doesn't make any sense, man.

00:06:00.141 --> 00:06:02.157
Why would I even have these premonitions

00:06:02.192 --> 00:06:04.597
Unless there was a chance that
I can stop them from happening.

00:06:04.632 --> 00:06:06.298
I don't know.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.174
So, what do you think killed him?

00:06:14.376 --> 00:06:16.081
Maybe the guy killed himself.

00:06:16.116 --> 00:06:19.109
Maybe there's nothing
supernatural going on at all.

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.824
I'm telling you. I watched it happen.

00:06:21.859 --> 00:06:24.504
He was murdered by something Dean.

00:06:24.539 --> 00:06:26.559
It trapped him in the garage.

00:06:26.594 --> 00:06:28.364
Like what? A spirit?
A poltergeist? What?

00:06:28.399 --> 00:06:29.856
I don't know what it was.

00:06:29.891 --> 00:06:32.085
I don't know why I'm
having these dreams.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.280
I don't know what the
hell is happening Dean.

00:06:34.555 --> 00:06:36.141
What?

00:06:36.176 --> 00:06:38.761
Nothing, man. I'm
just worried about you.

00:06:38.796 --> 00:06:40.867
Well, don't look at me like that.

00:06:40.902 --> 00:06:42.939
I'm not looking at you like anything.

00:06:43.163 --> 00:06:45.436
But I got to say. You look like crap.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:48.380
Nice, thanks. You welcome.

00:06:48.563 --> 00:06:51.355
Come on, let's just pick
this up in the morning.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.147
Check out the house,
we'll talk to the family.

00:06:54.607 --> 00:06:57.351
Dean, you saw them. They're devastated.

00:06:57.386 --> 00:07:00.095
They're not gonna want to talk to us.

00:07:01.517 --> 00:07:03.675
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:04.444 --> 00:07:07.005
But I think I know who they'll talk to.

00:07:08.079 --> 00:07:09.969
Who?

00:07:13.805 --> 00:07:16.770
This has got to be a
whole new loaf for us.

00:07:21.258 --> 00:07:22.940
Good afternoon.

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.560
I'm Father Simmons.
This is Father Freely.

00:07:25.595 --> 00:07:28.146
We're new junior priests
at Saint Augustine.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.989
May we come in?

00:07:31.137 --> 00:07:32.556
Thanks.

00:07:33.153 --> 00:07:35.143
We're very sorry for your loss.

00:07:37.046 --> 00:07:40.800
In difficult times like these when the
Lord's guidance is most needed. Look...

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:43.349
You want to pitch your whole
Lord has a plan thing fine.

00:07:43.384 --> 00:07:45.800
Don't pitch it to me. My brother's dead.

00:07:45.835 --> 00:07:48.386
Roger, please.

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:51.813
Excuse me.

00:07:54.364 --> 00:07:57.529
I'm sorry about my brother in law.

00:07:57.564 --> 00:08:00.695
He's just so upset about Jim's death.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.375
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.083
That'll be great.

00:08:07.136 --> 00:08:10.138
It was wonderful of you to stop by.

00:08:10.173 --> 00:08:12.846
The support of the church
means so much right now.

00:08:12.881 --> 00:08:14.049
Of course.

00:08:14.084 --> 00:08:17.302
After all, we all are god's children.

00:08:24.789 --> 00:08:25.912
What?

00:08:25.947 --> 00:08:30.019
Just tone it down a little bit, Father.

00:08:35.013 --> 00:08:36.649
So, Ms. Miller.

00:08:36.684 --> 00:08:39.684
Did your husband have
a history of depression?

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:41.501
Nothing like that.

00:08:41.536 --> 00:08:45.608
We... had our ups and
downs like everyone.

00:08:45.643 --> 00:08:48.054
But we were happy.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.234
I just don't understand

00:08:52.269 --> 00:08:55.740
How Jim could do something like that.

00:08:57.775 --> 00:09:01.424
I'm so sorry you had
to find him like that.

00:09:01.586 --> 00:09:03.814
Actually...

00:09:03.849 --> 00:09:06.042
Our son, Max.

00:09:06.519 --> 00:09:09.523
He was the one who found him.

00:09:09.558 --> 00:09:12.335
Do you mind if maybe...
I go talk to him?

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.529
No.

00:09:13.564 --> 00:09:15.773
Oh, thank you Father.

00:09:27.765 --> 00:09:29.078
Max?

00:09:29.113 --> 00:09:31.015
Hey, I'm Sam.

00:09:34.734 --> 00:09:37.691
Ms. Miller, you have a lovely home.

00:09:38.181 --> 00:09:41.226
How long have you lived here?

00:09:41.261 --> 00:09:44.271
We moved in about five years ago.

00:09:45.115 --> 00:09:47.942
You know, the only problem
with these old houses

00:09:47.977 --> 00:09:51.163
I bet you have all kinds of headaches.

00:09:51.198 --> 00:09:53.164
Like what?

00:09:53.199 --> 00:09:55.095
Well...

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.653
Weird leaks.

00:09:57.688 --> 00:09:59.827
Electrical shortages.

00:09:59.862 --> 00:10:03.789
Odd sort of noises at
night. That kind of things.

00:10:05.136 --> 00:10:07.935
No, nothing like that.

00:10:08.105 --> 00:10:10.370
It's been perfect.

00:10:16.268 --> 00:10:17.657
May I use your restroom?

00:10:17.692 --> 00:10:20.310
Oh, sure. It's just up the stairs.

00:10:20.345 --> 00:10:21.829
Okay.

00:10:24.998 --> 00:10:27.515
So, what was your dad like?

00:10:28.593 --> 00:10:30.861
Just a normal dad.

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.313
Yeah.

00:10:32.348 --> 00:10:35.573
You live at home now?

00:10:35.608 --> 00:10:37.186
Yeah.

00:10:37.221 --> 00:10:41.030
I'm trying to save up
for school but it's hard.

00:10:48.385 --> 00:10:51.795
So, when you found your dad?

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:55.102
I woke up.

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:58.782
I heard the engine running.

00:11:02.803 --> 00:11:05.744
I don't know why he did it.

00:11:09.088 --> 00:11:11.186
I know its ruff.

00:11:11.221 --> 00:11:13.250
Losing a parent.

00:11:13.285 --> 00:11:17.087
Especially when you don't
have all the answers.

00:12:12.159 --> 00:12:13.755
Anything?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.395
Zip.

00:12:18.499 --> 00:12:21.083
Escanaba Motel No Vacancy

00:12:23.926 --> 00:12:26.238
So, what do you have? Well, nothing.

00:12:26.273 --> 00:12:29.101
Nothing bad has happened to the
Miller house since it was built.

00:12:29.136 --> 00:12:31.213
What about the land? No
graveyard, battlefields,

00:12:31.248 --> 00:12:36.286
Tribal lands or any other kind of
atrocity on or near the property.

00:12:37.017 --> 00:12:39.043
Hey, man. I told you. I
searched the house up and down.

00:12:39.078 --> 00:12:42.879
There were no cold spots,
no soul person, nada.

00:12:43.366 --> 00:12:45.353
And the family said
everything was normal.

00:12:45.388 --> 00:12:47.306
Well, if there was a
demon or poltergeist.

00:12:47.341 --> 00:12:49.139
You don't think somebody
would have notice something?

00:12:49.174 --> 00:12:52.256
I used the infrared thermo
scanner, man. There was nothing.

00:12:52.291 --> 00:12:54.743
So what? You think Jim
Miller killed himself?

00:12:54.778 --> 00:12:59.585
And my dream was some sort
of freakish coincidence?

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:01.154
I don't know.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.635
I'm pretty sure there's nothing
supernatural about that house.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.256
Yeah.

00:13:06.291 --> 00:13:07.842
Well...

00:13:08.517 --> 00:13:10.656
You know, maybe...

00:13:10.691 --> 00:13:12.970
Maybe there's nothing
to do with the house.

00:13:13.005 --> 00:13:15.217
Maybe it's just a...

00:13:15.252 --> 00:13:18.577
Gosh. Maybe it's connected to Jim.

00:13:18.612 --> 00:13:20.821
In some other way.

00:13:20.856 --> 00:13:23.031
What's wrong with you?

00:13:24.764 --> 00:13:26.140
My head!

00:13:26.175 --> 00:13:27.517
Sam?

00:13:29.145 --> 00:13:30.173
Hey!

00:13:30.399 --> 00:13:31.641
Hey!

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:34.021
What's going on? Talk to me.

00:15:14.104 --> 00:15:15.620
It's happening again!

00:15:15.655 --> 00:15:17.964
Something's gonna kill Roger Miller.

00:15:23.242 --> 00:15:25.022
Roger Miller?

00:15:25.679 --> 00:15:28.578
No, no, just the address please.

00:15:29.949 --> 00:15:31.810
Okay, thanks.

00:15:33.121 --> 00:15:37.265
450 West Grove. Apartment 1120.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.074
You okay?

00:15:39.323 --> 00:15:42.841
Yeah. If you're goon hurl. I'll
pull the car over, you know.

00:15:42.876 --> 00:15:45.288
I'm fine. Just drive.

00:15:45.323 --> 00:15:46.951
All right.

00:15:49.943 --> 00:15:51.469
Dean, I'm scared man.

00:15:51.504 --> 00:15:53.168
These nightmares weren't bad enough.

00:15:53.203 --> 00:15:54.833
Now I'm seeing things when I'm awake?

00:15:54.868 --> 00:15:56.258
And theses...

00:15:56.293 --> 00:16:02.497
Visions or whatever. They're
getting intense, painful.

00:16:02.532 --> 00:16:04.016
Come on man. You'll be all right.

00:16:04.051 --> 00:16:07.198
You'll be fine. What
is it about the Millers?

00:16:07.233 --> 00:16:12.356
Why am I connected to them?
Why am I watching them die?

00:16:12.574 --> 00:16:14.884
Why the hell is this happening
to me? I don't know Sam.

00:16:14.919 --> 00:16:16.901
But we'll figure it out, okay?

00:16:16.936 --> 00:16:19.969
We face the unexplainable every
single day. This is just another thing.

00:16:20.004 --> 00:16:22.512
No. It's never been us.

00:16:22.547 --> 00:16:25.137
It's never been in the family like this.

00:16:25.172 --> 00:16:28.814
Tell the truth. You can't tell
me this doesn't freak you out.

00:16:31.549 --> 00:16:33.833
This doesn't freak me out.

00:16:42.981 --> 00:16:44.295
Hey, Roger!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.507
Hey, hold up a second.

00:16:45.542 --> 00:16:47.673
What are you guys,
missionaries? Leave me alone.

00:16:47.708 --> 00:16:49.227
Please!

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.105
Hey! Roger!

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.274
We're trying to help!
Please! Hey, hey, hey!

00:16:58.309 --> 00:17:00.026
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:00.297 --> 00:17:02.062
I don't want your help.

00:17:02.097 --> 00:17:03.782
We're not priests. You've
got to listen to us!

00:17:03.817 --> 00:17:06.118
Roger, you're in danger!

00:17:07.738 --> 00:17:09.210
Come on, come on.

00:18:13.541 --> 00:18:14.747
Here.

00:18:15.317 --> 00:18:16.543
Start wiping down your finger prints.

00:18:16.578 --> 00:18:17.666
We don't want the cops
to know we were here.

00:18:17.701 --> 00:18:19.576
Go! Go! Come on!

00:18:23.878 --> 00:18:25.852
I'm gonna take a look inside.

00:18:31.855 --> 00:18:33.481
I'm telling you there
was nothing in there.

00:18:33.516 --> 00:18:35.818
There's no signs either.
Just like the Miller's house.

00:18:35.853 --> 00:18:38.873
I saw something in the
vision. Like a dark shape.

00:18:38.908 --> 00:18:40.077
Something was...

00:18:40.112 --> 00:18:41.831
Something was stalking Roger.

00:18:41.866 --> 00:18:44.665
Well, whatever it was I'm sure
it's not connected to their house.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.862
No, it's connected to the family itself.

00:18:46.897 --> 00:18:49.335
So, what do you think?
Like a ventral spirit?

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.748
Oh, yeah. Few of them have been
known to ledge horn to families.

00:18:51.783 --> 00:18:53.356
They'll haunt them for years.

00:18:53.391 --> 00:18:56.142
Angier, Badges.

00:18:57.052 --> 00:18:58.522
Basically it was like a curse.

00:18:58.557 --> 00:19:01.158
Maybe Roger and Jim Miller got
involved in something heavy.

00:19:01.193 --> 00:19:04.337
Something curse worthy. And
now something's out for revenge.

00:19:04.372 --> 00:19:07.510
And they're making their family dying.

00:19:08.593 --> 00:19:11.345
Hey, you think Max is in danger?

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.062
Let's figure out before he is.

00:19:14.097 --> 00:19:17.324
Well... I know one thing I have
in common with these people.

00:19:17.359 --> 00:19:19.046
What's that?

00:19:19.081 --> 00:19:21.463
Well, their families are cursed.

00:19:21.498 --> 00:19:23.446
Our family's not cursed.

00:19:23.481 --> 00:19:26.832
We're just had our dark spots.

00:19:27.942 --> 00:19:29.497
Our dark spots are...

00:19:29.532 --> 00:19:31.656
Pretty dark.

00:19:31.691 --> 00:19:33.780
You're dark.

00:19:37.204 --> 00:19:41.054
My mom's resting. She's
pretty packed. Of course.

00:19:41.416 --> 00:19:44.633
All these people kept
coming with like casseroles.

00:19:44.668 --> 00:19:47.219
I finally had to tell
them all to go away.

00:19:47.254 --> 00:19:51.723
You know, cause nothing says
I'm sorry like a tuna casserole.

00:20:04.015 --> 00:20:06.532
How are you holding up?

00:20:06.714 --> 00:20:08.377
I'm okay.

00:20:08.412 --> 00:20:11.796
Your dad and your uncle were close?

00:20:11.831 --> 00:20:14.621
Yeah, I guess. They were brothers.

00:20:14.656 --> 00:20:17.377
I use to hang out when I was little.

00:20:17.412 --> 00:20:21.653
But not lately, much?
No, it's not that. It's...

00:20:21.688 --> 00:20:24.099
We used to be neighbors
when I was a kid.

00:20:24.134 --> 00:20:26.476
We lived across town
in this house and...

00:20:26.511 --> 00:20:31.252
Uncle Roger lived next door so
he was over all the time. Right.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:36.526
So how was it in that
house when you were a kid?

00:20:36.561 --> 00:20:38.719
It was fine.

00:20:39.296 --> 00:20:40.641
Why?

00:20:40.676 --> 00:20:43.052
All good memories?

00:20:43.087 --> 00:20:45.851
You remember anything unusual?

00:20:45.886 --> 00:20:50.264
Something involving your
father and your uncle maybe?

00:20:51.451 --> 00:20:53.434
Why do you...?

00:20:53.608 --> 00:20:56.141
Why do you ask?

00:20:57.765 --> 00:21:00.212
It's just a question.

00:21:01.769 --> 00:21:06.061
No, there was nothing.
We were totally normal.

00:21:06.964 --> 00:21:09.933
Happy. Good.

00:21:10.803 --> 00:21:13.504
That's good.

00:21:14.145 --> 00:21:16.615
Well, you must be exhausted.

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:19.086
We should take off. Right.

00:21:20.158 --> 00:21:23.565
Thanks. Yeah.

00:21:27.509 --> 00:21:29.860
Nobody's family is
totally normal and happy.

00:21:29.895 --> 00:21:32.212
You see when he was
talking about his old house?

00:21:32.247 --> 00:21:34.331
Sounded scared.

00:21:34.366 --> 00:21:36.268
Max isn't telling us everything.

00:21:36.303 --> 00:21:38.135
See we go find the old neighborhood?

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:40.891
Find out what life it
was with the Millers.

00:21:45.333 --> 00:21:47.173
Have you lived in the
neighborhood very long?

00:21:47.208 --> 00:21:48.831
Yeah, almost twenty years now.

00:21:48.866 --> 00:21:50.049
It's nice and quiet.

00:21:50.084 --> 00:21:51.198
Why you looking to buy?

00:21:51.233 --> 00:21:53.248
No, no, actually we
were just wondering if...

00:21:53.283 --> 00:21:57.048
If you might recall a family that use to
live right across the street I believe.

00:21:57.083 --> 00:21:59.454
Yeah, the Millers. They
had a little boy named Max.

00:21:59.489 --> 00:22:01.177
Right.

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.003
Yeah, I remember.

00:22:03.038 --> 00:22:05.971
Their brother had the place next door.

00:22:06.248 --> 00:22:08.409
So, what's this about?

00:22:08.444 --> 00:22:10.545
That poor kid okay?

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.646
What do you mean?

00:22:13.008 --> 00:22:16.118
Well, in my life. I've never
seen a child treated like that.

00:22:16.153 --> 00:22:17.452
I mean, I'd hear Mr. Miller

00:22:17.487 --> 00:22:20.872
Yelling and throwing things clear
across the street. He was a...

00:22:20.907 --> 00:22:22.616
Mean drunk.

00:22:22.651 --> 00:22:24.541
Used to beat the tire out of Max.

00:22:24.576 --> 00:22:28.329
Bruises. Broke his arm
two times that I know of.

00:22:28.364 --> 00:22:30.811
And this was going on regularly?

00:22:30.846 --> 00:22:32.607
Practically everyday.

00:22:32.642 --> 00:22:34.404
In fact that thug brother of his

00:22:34.439 --> 00:22:37.928
Was just as likely take a swing
at the boy. But the worst part...

00:22:37.963 --> 00:22:39.868
Was his step mother.

00:22:39.903 --> 00:22:42.085
She just...

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:45.466
Stand there, checked out. Never
lifted a finger to protect him.

00:22:45.501 --> 00:22:48.082
I must have called the
police seven or eight times.

00:22:48.117 --> 00:22:50.664
Never did any good. Now,
you said 'step mother'.

00:22:50.699 --> 00:22:53.723
I think his real mom
died. Some sort of...

00:22:53.758 --> 00:22:56.647
Accident. Car accident I think.

00:22:56.682 --> 00:22:58.848
Are you okay there?

00:23:00.631 --> 00:23:02.832
Uh, yeah. Thanks for your time.

00:23:02.867 --> 00:23:05.034
Oh, yeah. Thank you. Let's go.

00:23:06.096 --> 00:23:07.803
Oh, god.

00:23:19.419 --> 00:23:22.045
I don't know what you mean by that.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:25.319
You know I didn't do
anything. That's right.

00:23:25.354 --> 00:23:28.857
You didn't do anything.

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:33.219
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:23:33.748 --> 00:23:35.763
How did you...?

00:23:38.498 --> 00:23:41.106
Max! Please!

00:23:53.085 --> 00:23:58.077
But every time you
stood there and watched.

00:23:58.112 --> 00:24:01.379
Pretending it wasn't happening.

00:24:01.414 --> 00:24:04.646
I'm sorry. No, you're not.

00:24:05.126 --> 00:24:08.180
You just don't want to die.

00:24:21.010 --> 00:24:22.880
Max is doing it.

00:24:22.915 --> 00:24:25.013
Everything I've been seeing.

00:24:25.048 --> 00:24:28.037
Are you sure about
this? Yeah, I saw him.

00:24:28.212 --> 00:24:29.630
How is he pulling it off?

00:24:29.665 --> 00:24:31.591
I don't know. Looks like telekinesis.

00:24:31.626 --> 00:24:33.482
So, he's Psychic? He's a spoon bender?

00:24:33.517 --> 00:24:36.146
I didn't even realize but
this whole time he was there.

00:24:36.181 --> 00:24:38.521
He was outside of the
garage when his dad died.

00:24:38.556 --> 00:24:40.862
He was in the apartment
when his uncle died.

00:24:40.897 --> 00:24:42.354
His visions this whole time.

00:24:42.389 --> 00:24:46.099
I wasn't connected to the
Millers. I was connecting to Max.

00:24:46.276 --> 00:24:49.054
The thing I don't know
is why man. I guess...

00:24:49.089 --> 00:24:50.902
Cause we are so alike?

00:24:50.937 --> 00:24:53.748
What are you talking about?
Dude's nothing like you.

00:24:53.783 --> 00:24:56.172
Oh, we both have psychic abilities.

00:24:56.207 --> 00:24:57.817
We're both... Both what?

00:24:57.852 --> 00:24:59.392
Sam, Max is a monster.

00:24:59.427 --> 00:25:01.386
He's already killed two people
now he's going for a third.

00:25:01.421 --> 00:25:04.107
With all he went through. The beatings.

00:25:04.142 --> 00:25:05.502
To want revenge on those people.

00:25:05.537 --> 00:25:08.163
I'm sorry man, I hate to
say it. It's not that insane.

00:25:08.198 --> 00:25:10.687
Yeah, but it doesn't justify
murdering your entire family.

00:25:10.722 --> 00:25:13.176
Dean... He's no different than
anything else we've hunted.

00:25:13.211 --> 00:25:15.124
All right, we've got to end it.

00:25:16.155 --> 00:25:18.271
We're not gonna kill Max.

00:25:18.306 --> 00:25:19.527
Then what?

00:25:19.562 --> 00:25:21.794
I hand him over to the cops
and say Lock him up, officer.

00:25:21.829 --> 00:25:24.227
He kills with his power
of his mind. Forget it.

00:25:24.262 --> 00:25:26.877
No way man. Sam! Do...

00:25:26.912 --> 00:25:28.673
He's a person.

00:25:28.708 --> 00:25:30.021
We can talk to him.

00:25:30.056 --> 00:25:33.773
Hey! Promise me you'll
follow my lead on this one.

00:25:34.663 --> 00:25:36.285
All right, fine.

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:38.694
But I'm not letting
him hurt anyone else.

00:25:49.380 --> 00:25:53.338
You know I never did
anything. That's right.

00:25:53.373 --> 00:25:56.405
You didn't do anything.

00:25:56.682 --> 00:25:59.895
You didn't stop them. Not once.

00:26:00.991 --> 00:26:02.869
Fathers?

00:26:04.996 --> 00:26:08.332
What are you doing here? Oh...

00:26:08.367 --> 00:26:10.120
Sorry to interrupt.

00:26:10.155 --> 00:26:11.839
Max, could we uh...

00:26:11.874 --> 00:26:16.013
Could we talk to you
outside for just one second?

00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:19.287
About what?

00:26:19.322 --> 00:26:21.205
It's... It's private.

00:26:21.240 --> 00:26:24.016
Um... I wouldn't want to
bother your mother with it.

00:26:24.051 --> 00:26:27.026
We won't be long at
all though. I promise.

00:26:33.087 --> 00:26:34.528
Okay.

00:26:34.563 --> 00:26:35.969
Great.

00:27:02.117 --> 00:27:04.146
You're not priests!

00:27:10.245 --> 00:27:11.555
Max! What's happening?

00:27:11.590 --> 00:27:13.896
Shut up! What are you doing?

00:27:16.553 --> 00:27:18.843
I said shut up! Max, calm down.

00:27:18.878 --> 00:27:20.786
Who are you? We just
want to talk to you.

00:27:20.821 --> 00:27:22.695
Yeah, right. That's
why you brought this.

00:27:22.730 --> 00:27:24.389
That was a mistake, all right?

00:27:24.424 --> 00:27:26.651
So was lying about who we
were. But no more lying Max.

00:27:26.686 --> 00:27:28.480
Okay? Just please.

00:27:28.515 --> 00:27:31.762
Just hear me out. About what?

00:27:32.203 --> 00:27:34.847
I saw you do it.

00:27:34.882 --> 00:27:38.993
I saw you kill your dad and
your uncle before it happened.

00:27:39.028 --> 00:27:42.658
What? I'm having visions about you.

00:27:42.693 --> 00:27:44.550
You're crazy.

00:27:44.585 --> 00:27:46.842
So, you weren't gonna launch
a knife at your step mom?

00:27:46.877 --> 00:27:48.171
Right here?

00:27:48.206 --> 00:27:50.719
Isn't that hard to believe?
Max, look what you can do?

00:27:50.754 --> 00:27:53.630
Max, I was drawn here, all right?

00:27:54.207 --> 00:27:57.071
I think I'm here to help you.

00:27:59.943 --> 00:28:02.523
No one can help me.

00:28:02.558 --> 00:28:03.883
Let me try.

00:28:03.918 --> 00:28:05.330
We'll just talk.

00:28:05.365 --> 00:28:06.674
Me and you.

00:28:06.709 --> 00:28:10.938
We'll get Dean and Alice
out of here. No, no way.

00:28:11.651 --> 00:28:13.765
Nobody leaves this house!

00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:16.251
And nobody has to, all
right? They'll just...

00:28:16.286 --> 00:28:17.528
They'll just go upstairs.

00:28:17.563 --> 00:28:19.313
Sam, I'm not leaving you alone with him.

00:28:19.348 --> 00:28:20.961
Yes, you are.

00:28:20.996 --> 00:28:22.540
Look, Max...

00:28:22.575 --> 00:28:24.818
You're in charge here. All
right? We all know that.

00:28:24.853 --> 00:28:27.061
No one's gonna do anything
that you don't want to do.

00:28:27.096 --> 00:28:30.625
But I'm talking five
minutes here man. Sam...

00:28:33.242 --> 00:28:35.475
Five minutes?

00:28:36.553 --> 00:28:37.961
Go.

00:28:50.780 --> 00:28:52.147
Come on.

00:28:56.776 --> 00:28:58.199
Look.

00:28:58.234 --> 00:29:00.800
I can't begin to understand
what you went through.

00:29:00.835 --> 00:29:03.442
That's right, you can't. Max...

00:29:03.477 --> 00:29:05.960
This has to stop. It will.

00:29:05.995 --> 00:29:08.443
After my step mother... No.

00:29:08.478 --> 00:29:10.428
You need to let her go.

00:29:10.463 --> 00:29:12.235
Why?

00:29:13.189 --> 00:29:15.143
Did she beat you?

00:29:15.178 --> 00:29:16.493
No.

00:29:16.528 --> 00:29:21.126
But she never tried to save
me. She's part of it too.

00:29:22.356 --> 00:29:24.087
Look what they did to you.

00:29:24.122 --> 00:29:28.016
Look what they all
did to you growing up.

00:29:28.051 --> 00:29:31.911
They deserve to be punished. Growing up?

00:29:31.946 --> 00:29:34.806
Try last week.

00:29:40.295 --> 00:29:42.312
My dad still hits me.

00:29:42.347 --> 00:29:45.847
Just in places people wouldn't see it.

00:29:46.848 --> 00:29:49.994
Old habits die hard I guess.

00:29:53.720 --> 00:29:55.654
I'm sorry.

00:30:01.118 --> 00:30:05.017
When I first found out
I could move things.

00:30:05.052 --> 00:30:07.356
It was a gift.

00:30:07.840 --> 00:30:11.560
My whole life I was helpless.

00:30:11.595 --> 00:30:14.163
But now I have this.

00:30:15.030 --> 00:30:17.333
So, last week...

00:30:17.368 --> 00:30:19.602
Dad gets drunk.

00:30:19.637 --> 00:30:22.085
First time in a long time.

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:24.498
And he beats me to hell.

00:30:24.533 --> 00:30:27.274
It's the first time in a long time.

00:30:27.510 --> 00:30:30.225
And I do what I had to do.

00:30:30.260 --> 00:30:33.016
Why didn't you just leave?

00:30:33.051 --> 00:30:35.772
It isn't about getting away.

00:30:36.744 --> 00:30:40.868
Just knowing that they'd
still be out there.

00:30:41.151 --> 00:30:46.248
It was about not being afraid.

00:30:47.953 --> 00:30:50.736
When my dad used to look at me.

00:30:50.771 --> 00:30:53.484
There was hate in his eyes.

00:30:53.519 --> 00:30:57.061
Do you know what that feels like?

00:30:59.218 --> 00:31:00.481
No.

00:31:00.516 --> 00:31:03.609
He blamed me for everything.

00:31:03.644 --> 00:31:06.703
For his job. For his life.

00:31:06.738 --> 00:31:09.529
For my mom's death.

00:31:09.564 --> 00:31:12.876
Why did he blame you
for your mom's death?

00:31:15.498 --> 00:31:18.215
Because she died in my nursery.

00:31:18.250 --> 00:31:21.565
While I was asleep in my crib.

00:31:21.600 --> 00:31:24.881
As if that makes it my fault.

00:31:25.097 --> 00:31:27.145
She died in your nursery?

00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:28.389
Yeah.

00:31:28.424 --> 00:31:31.502
There was a fire and he get drunk

00:31:31.537 --> 00:31:35.602
And blab along like she
died in some insane way.

00:31:35.637 --> 00:31:38.029
He said that she burned up.

00:31:38.064 --> 00:31:40.895
Pinned to the ceiling.

00:31:46.017 --> 00:31:48.139
Listen to me Max.

00:31:48.609 --> 00:31:50.265
What your dad said.

00:31:50.300 --> 00:31:53.004
About what happened to your mom.

00:31:53.951 --> 00:31:56.203
It's real.

00:31:57.357 --> 00:31:59.053
What?

00:31:59.088 --> 00:32:01.105
It happened to my mom too.

00:32:01.140 --> 00:32:03.061
Exactly the same.

00:32:03.096 --> 00:32:04.947
My nursery, my crib.

00:32:04.982 --> 00:32:07.753
My dad saw her in the ceiling.

00:32:08.294 --> 00:32:11.674
Your dad must have been
as drunk as mine. No.

00:32:11.709 --> 00:32:13.571
No, it's the same thing, Max.

00:32:13.606 --> 00:32:15.831
The same thing killed our mothers.

00:32:15.866 --> 00:32:18.176
That's impossible.

00:32:18.525 --> 00:32:22.117
This must be why I've been
having visions during the day.

00:32:22.291 --> 00:32:24.674
Why they're getting more intense.

00:32:24.866 --> 00:32:28.308
Cause you and I must be
connected in some way.

00:32:28.490 --> 00:32:31.346
Your abilities started six,
seven months ago, right?

00:32:31.381 --> 00:32:33.193
Out of the blue?

00:32:33.469 --> 00:32:34.544
How'd you know that?

00:32:34.579 --> 00:32:36.603
Because that's when my
abilities started Max.

00:32:36.638 --> 00:32:39.218
I mean, yours seem to be much
further along but still this...

00:32:39.253 --> 00:32:41.444
This means something. Right?

00:32:41.479 --> 00:32:46.404
I mean, for some reason.
You and I were chosen.

00:32:48.119 --> 00:32:50.290
For what?

00:32:51.154 --> 00:32:53.162
I don't know.

00:32:53.909 --> 00:32:56.114
But Dean and I... My brother and I...

00:32:56.149 --> 00:32:58.320
We're hunting for your mom's killer.

00:32:58.355 --> 00:33:00.003
We can find answers.

00:33:00.038 --> 00:33:02.614
Answers that can answer us both.

00:33:02.649 --> 00:33:05.191
But you got to let us go Max.

00:33:05.533 --> 00:33:08.826
You got to let your step mother go.

00:33:21.693 --> 00:33:23.637
No.

00:33:24.140 --> 00:33:26.987
What they did to me.

00:33:27.022 --> 00:33:29.799
I still have nightmares.

00:33:29.834 --> 00:33:32.563
I'm still scared all the time. Like...

00:33:32.598 --> 00:33:35.042
I'm waiting for that next beating.

00:33:35.077 --> 00:33:39.076
I'm just tired of being scared.
If I do this, it'll be all over.

00:33:39.111 --> 00:33:40.689
No, don't you get it?

00:33:40.724 --> 00:33:41.807
It won't.

00:33:41.842 --> 00:33:43.614
The nightmares won't end Max.

00:33:43.649 --> 00:33:45.459
Not like this.

00:33:45.494 --> 00:33:47.270
There's just...

00:33:47.431 --> 00:33:49.400
More pain.

00:33:49.643 --> 00:33:52.276
And it makes you as bad as them.

00:33:53.075 --> 00:33:55.155
Max...

00:33:55.742 --> 00:33:59.326
You don't have to go
this all by yourself.

00:34:04.241 --> 00:34:06.409
I'm sorry.

00:34:07.119 --> 00:34:08.564
No!

00:34:09.346 --> 00:34:10.946
Max!

00:34:12.777 --> 00:34:14.222
No!

00:34:14.257 --> 00:34:15.667
Max!

00:34:40.511 --> 00:34:41.873
Max!

00:34:44.088 --> 00:34:45.679
Son of a...

00:34:47.403 --> 00:34:48.775
Max.

00:34:49.380 --> 00:34:50.949
Max.

00:34:54.208 --> 00:34:55.743
No.

00:35:04.472 --> 00:35:06.067
Max.

00:35:07.587 --> 00:35:09.724
Stay back.

00:35:10.084 --> 00:35:11.918
It's not about you.

00:35:11.953 --> 00:35:15.012
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:35:16.349 --> 00:35:17.996
Okay.

00:35:36.394 --> 00:35:37.683
No!

00:35:38.415 --> 00:35:39.998
No!

00:35:51.655 --> 00:35:53.522
Max...

00:35:54.421 --> 00:35:56.132
No.

00:35:56.518 --> 00:35:58.634
Stay back.

00:35:58.832 --> 00:36:00.534
It's not about you.

00:36:00.569 --> 00:36:04.064
If you want to kill. You got
to go through with me first.

00:36:04.873 --> 00:36:06.741
Okay.

00:36:08.442 --> 00:36:10.973
No, don't! Don't!

00:36:11.008 --> 00:36:13.505
Please! Please Max!

00:36:14.607 --> 00:36:16.137
Max...

00:36:16.172 --> 00:36:18.551
We can help you.

00:36:18.764 --> 00:36:21.715
But this... What you're doing...

00:36:21.936 --> 00:36:24.052
It's not the solution.

00:36:24.087 --> 00:36:27.400
It's not gonna fix anything.

00:36:37.477 --> 00:36:40.009
You're right.

00:36:42.667 --> 00:36:44.192
No!

00:36:54.597 --> 00:36:56.819
Max attacked me.

00:36:56.854 --> 00:36:59.627
He threatened me with a gun.

00:37:00.330 --> 00:37:02.261
And these two?

00:37:04.214 --> 00:37:06.272
They're...

00:37:06.307 --> 00:37:08.731
Family friends.

00:37:09.779 --> 00:37:14.380
I called them as soon as
Max arrived. I was scared.

00:37:14.570 --> 00:37:17.088
They tried to stop him.

00:37:17.123 --> 00:37:19.607
They fought for the gun.

00:37:19.807 --> 00:37:22.669
Where did Max hid the gun?

00:37:24.511 --> 00:37:27.863
I don't know. He...

00:37:27.898 --> 00:37:31.215
Showed up and he...

00:37:34.653 --> 00:37:36.955
It's all right, Mrs. Miller.

00:37:38.405 --> 00:37:41.698
I lost everyone.

00:37:42.803 --> 00:37:44.403
Okay.

00:37:44.739 --> 00:37:46.826
We'll give you a call if we
have any further questions.

00:37:46.861 --> 00:37:48.624
Thanks officer.

00:37:49.076 --> 00:37:50.499
Come on.

00:38:03.167 --> 00:38:05.906
Freggis said something else.

00:38:05.941 --> 00:38:08.578
Got him through it
somehow. Don't do that.

00:38:08.613 --> 00:38:10.811
Do what? Told you yourself.

00:38:10.846 --> 00:38:13.689
It wouldn't matter what you
said. Max was too far gone.

00:38:13.724 --> 00:38:16.532
When I think about how he
looked at me man right before...

00:38:16.726 --> 00:38:18.064
I should have done something.

00:38:18.099 --> 00:38:20.283
Come on, man. You risked your life.

00:38:20.318 --> 00:38:23.725
I mean, yeah. If we gotten
there twenty years earlier...

00:38:25.626 --> 00:38:27.380
Well, I'll tell you one thing.

00:38:27.415 --> 00:38:29.551
We're lucky we had dad.

00:38:32.171 --> 00:38:35.728
I never thought you say that.

00:38:35.931 --> 00:38:37.205
Well...

00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:39.862
He could have gone away more after mom.

00:38:39.897 --> 00:38:45.393
A little more tequila a
little less demon hunting.

00:38:45.428 --> 00:38:48.860
Then we would have Max's childhood.

00:38:49.945 --> 00:38:52.355
All things considered.

00:38:52.390 --> 00:38:54.766
We turned out okay.

00:38:54.801 --> 00:38:57.116
Thanks to him.

00:39:00.817 --> 00:39:03.016
All things considered.

00:39:12.155 --> 00:39:13.411
Dean, I've been thinking.

00:39:13.446 --> 00:39:14.632
That's never a good thing.

00:39:14.667 --> 00:39:17.584
I'm serious. I've been thinking...

00:39:17.619 --> 00:39:21.328
Why would this demon or
whatever it is. Why would it...

00:39:21.363 --> 00:39:23.786
Kill mom and Jessica and Max's mother?

00:39:23.821 --> 00:39:25.409
You know, what does it want?

00:39:25.444 --> 00:39:27.643
No idea. Well, you think maybe...

00:39:27.678 --> 00:39:30.615
It was after us? After...

00:39:30.650 --> 00:39:33.457
Max and me? Why would you think that?

00:39:33.690 --> 00:39:34.964
I mean...

00:39:34.999 --> 00:39:36.962
Either telekinesis are premonitions.

00:39:36.997 --> 00:39:38.891
We both had abilities, you know.

00:39:38.926 --> 00:39:41.063
Maybe it was after us for some reason.

00:39:41.098 --> 00:39:44.212
Sam, if it wanted you. It
would have just taken you.

00:39:44.247 --> 00:39:45.398
Okay?

00:39:45.433 --> 00:39:47.010
This is not your fault.

00:39:47.045 --> 00:39:48.829
It is not about you.

00:39:48.864 --> 00:39:50.613
Then what is it about?

00:39:50.812 --> 00:39:53.289
It's about that damn thing
that did this to our family.

00:39:53.324 --> 00:39:56.072
That thing that we're gonna
find that thing we're gonna kill.

00:39:56.107 --> 00:39:58.218
And that's all.

00:39:59.497 --> 00:40:01.920
Actually, there's a...

00:40:01.955 --> 00:40:04.343
Something else too.

00:40:04.969 --> 00:40:06.346
Oh, geez what?

00:40:06.381 --> 00:40:09.584
When Max locked me in that closet.

00:40:09.619 --> 00:40:12.787
That big cabinet against the door.

00:40:13.139 --> 00:40:15.138
I moved it.

00:40:16.157 --> 00:40:19.016
Yeah, you're a little more up the body
strength than I gave you credit for.

00:40:19.051 --> 00:40:22.028
No man. I moved it. Like...

00:40:22.063 --> 00:40:24.164
Max.

00:40:26.908 --> 00:40:28.717
Oh.

00:40:30.636 --> 00:40:32.590
Right.

00:40:32.625 --> 00:40:34.544
Yeah.

00:40:41.233 --> 00:40:43.401
Bend this.

00:40:43.640 --> 00:40:45.312
I can't turn it on and off Dean.

00:40:45.347 --> 00:40:46.775
Then how'd you do it? I don't know.

00:40:46.810 --> 00:40:48.939
I can't control it. I just...

00:40:48.974 --> 00:40:52.511
I saw you die and it just came
out of me like a... Like a punch.

00:40:52.546 --> 00:40:53.827
You know, like a...

00:40:53.862 --> 00:40:56.633
Like a freak adrenaline thing.

00:41:00.276 --> 00:41:02.778
Well, I'm sure it won't happen again.

00:41:04.534 --> 00:41:06.266
Yeah, maybe.

00:41:06.301 --> 00:41:07.430
Aren't you worried man?

00:41:07.465 --> 00:41:10.143
Aren't you worried that I can
turn into Max or something?

00:41:10.178 --> 00:41:12.889
Nope. No way.

00:41:13.078 --> 00:41:14.273
You know why?

00:41:14.308 --> 00:41:15.959
No, why?

00:41:15.994 --> 00:41:18.230
Cause you got one advantage
that Max didn't have.

00:41:18.265 --> 00:41:19.983
Dad?

00:41:20.154 --> 00:41:22.392
Because dad's not here, Dean.

00:41:22.427 --> 00:41:24.070
No.

00:41:24.666 --> 00:41:26.748
Me.

00:41:27.897 --> 00:41:29.591
As long as I'm around...

00:41:29.626 --> 00:41:32.384
Nothing bad is gonna happen to you.

00:41:33.956 --> 00:41:35.653
Now then.

00:41:35.688 --> 00:41:38.526
I know what we need to
do with your premonitions.

00:41:38.561 --> 00:41:40.549
I know where we've got to go.

00:41:40.584 --> 00:41:42.599
Where?

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:44.924
Vegas.

00:41:48.769 --> 00:41:51.088
What? Come on man.

00:41:51.285 --> 00:41:54.411
Craps table. We'd clean up.



00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.000
